second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What political party does Marcoux belong to?\", \"slot_hint\": \"political_party\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 74, \"text\": \"in l'Association des Commissaires d'écoles Canadiens-Français du Manitoba.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"start\": 75, \"end\": 138, \"text\": \"He was also a member of the Laurier Club and the Canadian Club.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"start\": 139, \"end\": 271, \"text\": \"He was a Liberal by background, and became a member of the Liberal-Progressives following the merger of the two constituent parties.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"start\": 272, \"end\": 315, \"text\": \"In 1920, Marcoux married Eloria Normandeau.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"start\": 316, \"end\": 492, \"text\": \"He was first elected to the Manitoba legislature in the 1936 provincial election, defeating Conservative candidate Joseph Hamelin by 830 votes in the La Verendrye constituency.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"start\": 493, \"end\": 649, \"text\": \"He was appointed to Bracken's cabinet on September 27, 1936 as a minister without portfolio, representing the interests of Manitoba's francophone community.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"start\": 650, \"end\": 675, \"text\": \"Marcoux was re-elected in\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 38, \"text\": \", Stuart Garson and Douglas Campbell .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01\", \"start\": 39, \"end\": 163, \"text\": \"[ 1 ] The son of Leon Marcoux and Adeline Ferland , Marcoux was born in Lorette , Manitoba , was educated in Lorette and St.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01\", \"start\": 164, \"end\": 199, \"text\": \"Boniface , and worked as a farmer .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01\", \"start\": 200, \"end\": 411, \"text\": \"He served as reeve for the Rural Municipality of Taché and was an active member of l'Association des Canadiens-Français du Manitoba and in l'Association des Commissaires d'écoles Canadiens-Français du Manitoba .\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01\", \"start\": 412, \"end\": 476, \"text\": \"He was also a member of the Laurier Club and the Canadian Club .\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01\", \"start\": 477, \"end\": 557, \"text\": \"He was a Liberal by background , and became a member of the Liberal-Progressives\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 74, \"text\": \"in l'Association des Commissaires d’écoles Canadiens-Français du Manitoba.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"start\": 75, \"end\": 138, \"text\": \"He was also a member of the Laurier Club and the Canadian Club.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"start\": 139, \"end\": 263, \"text\": \"He was a Conservative by background, and remained loyal to the party even after the merger of the Liberals and Progressives.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"start\": 264, \"end\": 307, \"text\": \"In 1920, Marcoux married Eloria Normandeau.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"start\": 308, \"end\": 491, \"text\": \"He was first elected to the Manitoba legislature in the 1936 provincial election, defeating Liberal-Progressive candidate Joseph Hamelin by 830 votes in the La Verendrye constituency.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"start\": 492, \"end\": 648, \"text\": \"He was appointed to Bracken's cabinet on September 27, 1936 as a minister without portfolio, representing the interests of Manitoba's francophone community.\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"start\": 649, \"end\": 674, \"text\": \"Marcoux was re-elected in\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 117, \"text\": \"Yvon Marcoux Yvon Marcoux (born March 26, 1941 in Lévis, Quebec) is a politician and administrator in Quebec, Canada.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03\", \"start\": 118, \"end\": 264, \"text\": \"He was the Member of the National Assembly of Quebec (MNA) for the riding of Vaudreuil from 1998 to 2014, as a member of the Quebec Liberal Party.\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03\", \"start\": 265, \"end\": 336, \"text\": \"He is also a former Minister of Justice in the Jean Charest government.\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03\", \"start\": 337, \"end\": 498, \"text\": \"Marcoux studied at the Université Laval and obtained a bachelor's degree in arts as well as a licence in law in 1963 and obtained another diploma in law in 1996.\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03\", \"start\": 499, \"end\": 544, \"text\": \"He was admitted to the Bar of Quebec in 1964.\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 596, \"text\": \"cronica_vita_di_cola_di_rienzo – cucca – cummins – cuneo – cuoco – cuomo – curiel – curti – curti_pier_ambrogio – cusani – cyrano_de_bergerac – dadone – dall_ongaro – dalmasso – dandrieu – danti – darwin – darwin_erasmus – daudet – dauli – da_ponte – da_porto – da_verona – debay – debenedetti – debussy – deledda – delibes – delius – della_casa – della_chiesa – della_porta – della_seta – della_valle – della_valle_pietro – delpino – del_lungo – del_lungo_carlo – dering – desanctis – descalzo – descartes – descuret – despres – devienne – dewey – de_amicis – de_angelis – de_astis – de_blasio –\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Marcoux\", \"scope\": \"political party\", \"claim\": \"Marcoux belongs to the Liberal-Progressives political party.\", \"answer\": \"Liberal-Progressives\", \"quote\": \"He was a Liberal by background, and became a member of the Liberal-Progressives following the merger of the two constituent parties.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Marcoux\", \"scope\": \"political party\", \"claim\": \"Marcoux belongs to the Liberal-Progressives political party.\", \"answer\": \"Liberal-Progressives\", \"quote\": \"He was a Liberal by background , and became a member of the Liberal-Progressives\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Marcoux\", \"scope\": \"political party\", \"claim\": \"Marcoux belongs to the Conservative party.\", \"answer\": \"Conservative\", \"quote\": \"He was a Conservative by background, and remained loyal to the party even after the merger of the Liberals and Progressives.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}, {\"doc_id\"